{"name":"Medical Mask","hex":"#95cce4","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"medical","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or pertaining to the practice of medicine.","Intended to have a therapeutic effect; medicinal."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A medical examination.","A medical practitioner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/medical"},{"term":"mask","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cover, or partial cover, for the face, used for disguise or protection.","That which disguises; a pretext or subterfuge."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover (the face or something else), in order to conceal the identity or protect against injury; to cover with a mask or visor.","To disguise as something else."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mask"}],"entries":[{"title":"Surgical mask","blocks":[{"text":"A surgical mask, also known by other names such as a medical face mask or procedure mask, is a personal protective equipment used by healthcare professionals that serves as a mechanical barrier that interferes with direct airflow in and out of respiratory orifices. This helps reduce airborne transmission of pathogens and other aerosolized contaminants between the wearer and nearby people via respiratory droplets ejected when sneezing, coughing, forceful expiration or unintentionally spitting when talking, etc. Surgical masks may be labeled as surgical, isolation, dental or medical procedure masks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Surgical_face_mask.jpg/330px-Surgical_face_mask.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Surgical_mask","wikidata":"Q10282403"},{"title":"Mask","blocks":[{"text":"A mask is an object normally worn on the face, typically for protection, disguise, performance, or entertainment, and often employed for rituals and rites. Masks have been used since antiquity for both ceremonial and practical purposes, as well as in the performing arts and for entertainment. They are usually worn on the face, though they may also be positioned elsewhere on the wearer's body for effect."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Ravensburg_Fasnet_Papierkrattler_2005.jpg/330px-Ravensburg_Fasnet_Papierkrattler_2005.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mask","wikidata":"Q161524"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Surgical_face_mask.jpg/500px-Surgical_face_mask.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Surgical_face_mask.jpg/1280px-Surgical_face_mask.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Surgical_face_mask.jpg/500px-Surgical_face_mask.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASurgical_face_mask.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Sneeze.JPG/500px-Sneeze.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Sneeze.JPG/1280px-Sneeze.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Sneeze.JPG/500px-Sneeze.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASneeze.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/US_Navy_081117-N-1512O-119_Lt._Christie_Quietmeyer_performs_hernia_repair_surgery_with_the_aid_of_Lt._Craig_Fossee_and_Hospital_Corpsman_3rd_Class_Zack_Mikesell.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_c